.env
__pycache__/
# Your actual resume. resume.txt used to be committed here, complete with a
# real phone number, on a public repository.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Unanchored, "resume.pdf" matches at
# every depth, and it silently swallowed tests/fixtures/resume.pdf — the suite
# passed locally and failed on a fresh clone with nine missing-file errors.
# The file this is guarding is the one roaster.py reads by default, and that is
# at the repo root.
/resume.txt
/resume.pdf
/resume.docx
*.resume.txt

# ...but the test fixtures are meant to be committed. They are synthetic.
!tests/fixtures/
